.Language=English,English
.PluginContents=Context-dependent help

@Contents
$^#Context-dependent help for Far Manager 1.6x. Version 1.5.0, 20 Mar 2000.#
$^#Copyright (c) 1999-2000 Valentin Skirdin#.
 This Plugin Works with Far's Editor (basically), and Is shell around calling the functions #WinHelp# and #HtmlHelp#. Plugin Activation outside of the editor (from the disk menu or plugin menu) allows to cause only contents of help or topic, which was caused last.

 Why, ask You - answer. This possibility I did not get in editor (provided that ambience of development is FAR and command line, naturally except FoxPro :-). But to look a help, I was to start IDE or... in any event exit editor.

 Plugin in the same way remembers last parameters: keyword and number of file of help.

 Plugin in the same way is an ~activator~@Activator@ for calling URL-applications.

 ~What new?~@whatnew@
 ~How to install plugin?~@SetUp@
 ~How to work with plugin?~@Working@
 ~That is a WORD?~@IsWord@
 ~Благодарности~@Thank@
 ~About Author~@Author@

@whatnew
$^#What new?#
 - Entered notion "#Filename of help#" (that must be displayed in menu of choice of help)

 - Ways to files of help "have moved" from LNG-files in `cdHelps.msg

 ───
 ~Contents~@Contents

@SetUp
$^#How to install plugin?#
 1. Create in folder far\plugins\editor catalogue cdHelps
 2. Unpacked there archive
 3. Exit from FAR, file find in explorer ~HotKey_F1.reg~@HotKey_F1reg@, Double-Click mouse on this file...
 4. Start FAR
 5. ~Begin to edit file~@Working@

 In `cdHelps.msg' file conducted 20 positions for writing a full way to HLP- and CHM-files. Write all that you needed and get an enjoyment... :-)


 ───
 ~Contents~@Contents

@HotKey_F1reg
$^#HotKey_F1.reg#
 Here is this and be #HotKey_F1.reg#:

 REGEDIT4

 ; Context-dependent help
 [HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Far\KeyMacros\Editor\CtrlF1]
 "Sequence"="F11 ? ?"
 "DisableOutput"=dword:00000001

 ; Previous topic
 [HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Far\KeyMacros\Editor\AltF1]
 "Sequence"="F11 ? !"
 "DisableOutput"=dword:00000001

 ; Choise Help
 [HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Far\KeyMacros\Editor\ShiftF1]
 "Sequence"="F11 ?"
 "DisableOutput"=dword:00000001

 You may change this macro on its. On the taste and colour, how speak...


 ───
 ~Contents~@Contents

@Activator
$^#Activator of URL-applications#
 Plugin supports in the same way possibility of calling URL-applications from the editor. Under URL-applications are understood such applications, which support following protocols:

 ■ Protocol of access to files
   #file:#//C:\Program Files\Far\License.xUSSR.txt
 ■ FTP Protocol
   #ftp:#//ftp.kgb.ru/WinUtil/Rar/
 ■ HTTP Protocol
   #http:#//www.uic.nnov.ru/~~ruiv/plugring/
 ■ MailTo Protocol
   #mailto:#vskirdin@@mail.ru
 ■ News Protocol
   #news:#//fido7.far.support
 ■ Telnet Protocol
   #telnet:#//fido7.far.support
 ■ ...


 10 positions in LNG-files intended for these whole. Information for starting concrete exhibit get from roll ("HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT\#PROTOCOL#\shell\open\command").

 For activations URL-applications it is necessary to select block (together with prefix of protocol, naturally) and press ~Ctrl-F1~@HotKey_F1reg@.


 ───
 ~Contents~@Contents

@Working
$^#How to work with plugin "cdHelps"?#
 If You will use file ~HotKey_F1.reg~@HotKey_F1reg@, will be able to use following keys:

 ■ #Ctrl-F1#  - shows context-dependent help for current help file
 ■ #Alt-F1#   - shows section, which You called last
 ■ #Shift-F1# - allows to choose necessary HLP-file from list

 Plugin Can work in two modes:

 - set cursor on needed word and press #Ctrl-F1#. What Is A "WORD" in notions of plugin read ~here~@IsWord@.
 - select block (for instance <#stdio.h#>) and press #Ctrl-F1#;

 Having selected, for instance, line #mailto:Valentin Skirdin <vskirdin@@mail.ru>?Subject=cdHelps#, You will be able to actuate EMail client (See also ~Activator of URL-applications~@Activator@)

 ───
 ~Contents~@Contents

@IsWord
$^#That is a WORD?#
 Ops! Complex question. All think on different. Plugin always considers word as a collection of numerals, latin letters and symbol of underlining '_': #0-9#, #A-Z#, #a-z#, '#_#'. But You may assign additional symbols.

 In `cdHelps.msg' are two sections, have charge of logic of recognitions of words:

 #CharWordAdd# - That is considered by the word.
    If needed expand a notion "Word", sufficiently prescribe
    necessary symbols and overload FAR Manager.

 #IsSkipNoWord# - If this field = "1", then act rule
    #"Skip all symbols, not refering on word"#
    i.e. space and etc., and get to word.
    Default - 1. Set the "0" You hereunder close this
    possibility.

 ───
 ~Contents~@Contents

@CHMHelp
$^#CHM-файлы помощи#
@+
 CHM-files of help - a fashionable innovation of last years. Short - collected
in one file (with the extension .CHM) several HTML-files and named #HTML-based help#.

 If You installed by MSIE >= 4-й versions or You once upon a time installing
#HTML Help Workshop#, Your Windows capable to display like files of help.

 If plugin not show a topic from such files of help, here possible only 2 variants of
deciding a problem:

 a) in Your operating system not installed support for "HTML-based help"

 b) installing such support was "crooked"

 As be?

 For the event "a" You install MSIE >= 4.0 or "Microsoft HTML Help Workshop".
For the event "b" try to install "Microsoft HTML Help Workshop".
Logic of functioning a plugin at the show of topic from CHM-a file such a that
if it (plugin) does not find in the registry of record with the key
#CLSID\{ADB880A6-D8FF-11CF-9377-00AA003B7A11}#, or specified in this key of
file does not exist (not on the place it), is considered that not supports a
CHM-files!

 "Microsoft HTML Help Workshop" possible load with Web-site Microsoft companies.

 On my computer: hhctrl.ocx 4.74.8702 (InternalName - HHCtrl 1.3), so, if what bugs - inform me.

